  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Includes Catullus' poem 101, an elegy for his brother. The author defines and annotates each word of the poem, one word per page, on most of the left-hand pages.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Accordion-folded pages attached to heavy card stock. Issued in a drop spine box.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Condition: no library markings, in protective enclosure.</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Presents a facsimile of a book the author created after the death of her brother, and includes poetry, family photographs, letters, and sketches that deal with coming to terms with the loss.</subfield>
  </datafield>
